emma":"גָּרָה","tr":"ga·rah","gloss":"to stir up","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":14},{"base":"H3425","lemma":"יְרֻשָּׁה","tr":"ye·rush·shah","gloss":"possession","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":14},{"base":"H3423","lemma":"יָרַשׁ","tr":"ya·rash","gloss":"to possess: possess","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":231},{"base":"H7497","lemma":"רָפָה","tr":"ra·pah","gloss":"Rapha","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":25},{"base":"H5983","lemma":"עַמּוֹן","tr":"am·mon","gloss":"Ammon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":106},{"base":"H2490","lemma":"חָלַל","tr":"cha·lal","gloss":"to bore","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":143},{"base":"H4421","lemma":"מִלְחָמָה","tr":"mil·cha·mah","gloss":"battle","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":319}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":11,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"No man will be able to stand against you; the LORD your God will put the fear and dread of you upon all the land, wherever you set foot, as He has promised you.","from":25},{"book":"EXO","chapter":15,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"The nations will hear and tremble; anguish will grip the dwellers of Philistia.","from":25},{"book":"EXO","chapter":15,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"and terror and dread will fall on them. By the power of Your arm they will be as still as a stone until Your people pass by, O LORD, until the people You have bought pass by.","from":25},{"book":"DEU","chapter":28,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Then all the peoples of the earth will see that you are called by the name of the LORD, and they will stand in awe of you.","from":25},{"book":"EXO","chapter":23,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"I will send My terror ahead of you and throw into confusion every nation you encounter. I will make all your enemies turn and run.","from":25},{"book":"DEU","chapter":2,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Then the LORD said to me, “Do not harass the Moabites or provoke them to war, for I will not give you any of their land, because I have given Ar to the descendants of Lot as their possession.”","from":19},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"the Pathrusites, the Casluhites (from whom the Philistines came), and the Caphtorites.","from":23},{"book":"JOS","chapter":2,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"and said to them, “I know that the LORD has given you this land and that the fear of you has fallen on us, so that all who dwell in the land are melting in fear of you.","from":25}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"26-37":{"people":[{"id":"sihon-h5511","name":"Sihon","kind":"person","brief":"Amorite king","count":4,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"esau-h6215g","name":"Esau","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":29}],"places":[{"id":"heshbon-h2809","name":"Heshbon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"kedemoth-h6932","name":"Kedemoth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"ar-h6144","name":"Ar","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"jordan-h3383","name":"Jordan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"seir-h8165a","name":"Seir","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"jahaz-h3096","name":"Jahaz","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"arnon-h0769","name":"Arnon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":36},{"id":"aroer-h6177h","name":"Aroer","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":36},{"id":"gilead-h1568g","name":"Gilead","kind":"place","brief":"In Manasseh","count":1,"firstVerse":36},{"id":"ammon-h5983","name":"Ammon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":37},{"id":"jabbok-h2999","name":"Jabbok","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":37}],"words":[{"base":"H5511","lemma":"סִיחוֹן","tr":"si·chon","gloss":"Sihon","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":37},{"base":"H5892","lemma":"עִיר","tr":"ir","gloss":"excitement","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":1090},{"base":"H7535","lemma":"רַק","tr":"raq","gloss":"except","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":109},{"base":"H5674","lemma":"עָבַר","tr":"a·var","gloss":"to pass","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":556},{"base":"H5158","lemma":"נַ֫חַל","tr":"na·chal","gloss":"torrent: river","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":141},{"base":"H2809","lemma":"חֶשְׁבּוֹן","tr":"chesh·bon","gloss":"Heshbon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":38},{"base":"H3920","lemma":"לָכַד","tr":"la·khad","gloss":"to capture","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":121},{"base":"H2490","lemma":"חָלַל","tr":"cha·lal","gloss":"to bore","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":143},{"base":"H3423","lemma":"יָרַשׁ","tr":"ya·rash","gloss":"to possess: possess","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":231},{"base":"H9035","lemma":"נוּ","tr":"nu","gloss":"us","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":272}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NUM","chapter":21,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"But Sihon would not let Israel pass through his territory. Instead, he gathered his whole army and went out to confront Israel in the wilderness. When he came to Jahaz, he fought against Israel.","from":30},{"book":"EXO","chapter":4,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The LORD instructed Moses, “When you go back to Egypt, see that you perform before Pharaoh all the wonders that I have put within your power. But I will harden his heart so that he will not let the people go.","from":30},{"book":"JOS","chapter":13,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The area from Aroer on the rim of the Arnon Valley, along with the city in the middle of the valley, the whole plateau of Medeba as far as Dibon,","from":36},{"book":"GEN","chapter":32,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"During the night Jacob got up and took his two wives, his two maidservants, and his eleven sons, and crossed the ford of the Jabbok.","from":37},{"book":"NUM","chapter":20,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"“We will stay on the main road,” the Israelites replied, “and if we or our herds drink your water, we will pay for it. There will be no problem; only let us pass through on foot.”","from":28},{"book":"NUM","chapter":21,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And Israel put him to the sword and took possession of his land, from the Arnon to the Jabbok—but only up to the border of the Ammonites, because it was fortified.","from":37},{"book":"DEU","chapter":3,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So at that time we took possession of this land. To the Reubenites and Gadites I gave the land beyond Aroer along the Arnon Valley, and half the hill country of Gilead, along with its cities.","from":36},{"book":"DEU","chapter":3,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"and to the Reubenites and Gadites I gave the territory from Gilead to the Arnon Valley (the middle of the valley was the border) and up to the Jabbok River, the border of the Ammonites.","from":37}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}